## multi_documentation_hub_and_forum_view

### Current Progress
- **Reference and architecture discovery** - ✅ Complete
- **Documentation schema and backend domain** - ⬜ Not started
- **Shared documentation shell and editor boundary** - ⬜ Not started
- **Multi-documentation routes and management** - ⬜ Not started
- **Forum documentation adapter** - ⬜ Not started
- **Discovery, verification, and specs** - ⬜ Not started

The 2026-08-17 planner pass inspected the standalone `integrate/` documentation
shell, Skaia route/layout/feature contracts, forum models and APIs, the existing
TipTap editor and sanitized renderer, forum view modes, migration/lifecycle
policy, WebSocket conventions, and current specs. No overlapping documentation
todo or existing documentation backend domain was found.

The handoff treats `integrate/` as a UX reference only. `/doc` owns new
documentation records through a dedicated backend domain; `/forum/docs` is a
separate presentation adapter over authoritative forum categories and threads.

### Next Steps
- [ ] Use `.routines/worker` to validate the proposed route/schema contract and
  implement `036_documentation_hub.sql` plus documentation repository tests.
- [ ] Implement and verify the documentation handler/service/repositories,
  ownership, visibility, lifecycle, search, ordering, cache, events, and
  content-free realtime invalidation.
- [ ] Extract the shared TipTap boundary and build the Skaia-tokenized responsive
  documentation shell without importing the reference corpus or app shell.
- [ ] Implement `/doc` multi-set catalog, nested guide routes, inline management,
  dirty/conflict protection, search, navigation, and realtime refetch.
- [ ] Implement `/forum/docs/...` through forum-owned read projections and
  existing forum mutations, then prove storage and route separation.
- [ ] Complete backend/frontend/manual gates and update every affected compact
  spec before marking phases complete.

